// A line the interpreter has no scenario for, and NOTHING RUNS BEFORE IT:
// check.sh asserts both, so the "before" above it must never reach the screen.
//
// REBASED 2026-09-16, and the rebase is the point. This file used to declare a
// satellite.variable.string, which was refused because the string was not built.
// satelliteObject made it the interpreter's own string that day, so the line
// started working and this check went green for the wrong reason -- it was
// asserting an ABSENCE, and the absence was filled in.
//
// REBASED AGAIN 2026-09-22, from satellite.variable.float, when the author asked
// for the float, the hex, the colour and the fraction at once and all four became
// words a declaration may use. satellite.variable.time (word 1 6 3) is still
// unbuilt. When it is built this file goes red again, and the fix is the same
// one: move it to whatever is still unbuilt, not to delete the check.
satellite.include(satellite)

satellite.capsule satellite.main(satellite.container.list<satellite.variable.string> arguments)
{
    satellite.console.display("before")
    satellite.variable.time f = 1
    satellite.return(satellite)
}
